WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions of "Pyruvate Dehydrogenase" by Drew Berry, wehi.tv, for HHMI BioInteractive, from the film's page on YouTube (youtu.be/rSPUYA3gWK8).
Each cue is one line here, and mishearings in the captions are put right (plans/follow-the-molecule/captions.py lists them).

1
00:00:01.872 --> 00:00:04.990
The product of glycolysis.

2
00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:09.520
The pyruvate molecule is the source of carbon and electrons

3
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.390
for aerobic respiration reactions

4
00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:16.740
inside your mitochondria.

5
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:21.180
Pyruvate enters pores on the mitochondrial membrane,

6
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.640
and is transported into the interior.

7
00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:33.770
The reactions linking pyruvate with aerobic respiration

8
00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:38.090
are performed by huge protein complex

9
00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:42.350
made with multiple copies of three types of enzyme.

10
00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.760
The first enzyme catalyzes decarboxylation,

11
00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.790
transforming three carbon pyruvate

12
00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:04.680
into a two carbon acetyl group generating carbon dioxide

13
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:05.234
as a waste.

14
00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:12.400
The acetyl group is then grabbed by the second enzyme,

15
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.850
using flexible arms to efficiently transfer

16
00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:18.250
the product between reaction sites.

17
00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:28.960
In the active site of the second enzyme,

18
00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:31.600
the acetyl group is attached to coenzyme

19
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:37.625
A, generating acetyl CoA, fuel for the citric acid cycle.

20
00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:46.780
Two electrons from pyruvate oxidation

21
00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.410
are retained by the second enzyme,

22
00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:55.660
before passing them to coenzyme NADH, catalyzed

23
00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:58.480
by the third enzyme.

24
00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:02.740
Coenzyme NADH travels through the matrix,

25
00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:06.340
delivering electrons for the electron transport chain.

26
00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:26.090
In a sequence of reaction steps the pyruvate dehydrogenase

27
00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:31.100
enzyme complex generates fuel for aerobic respiration

28
00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:34.100
reactions, of the citric acid cycle

29
00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:37.360
and the electron transport chain.
